A||||5||kevin||dash board and gauges||||5||
Z||000000||kevin||03-25-2000||06:19 PM||||I have an aquaintance who is willing to sell me the GT dashboard which includes the gauge clusters in front of the steering wheel and the two extra gauges sitting atop the center console. Both the tach and speedometer indicate higher numbers than what my dash shows, because I have a 85 Duke. I believe the gauge cluster for the center console was available only on 6 cyl. GT's. Would there be any significant work involved in converting the GT dash to my SE? Would this be a simple remove and replace afternoon job? If not, what's involved? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||03-25-2000||06:40 PM||||The main instrument cluster (speedo, tach, etc) is a plug-n-play.  The Rally gauges (center pod) probably has to be wired in as it's unlikely (but possible) that you have the correct harness plug.  Do a quick search and you'll come up with the wiring directions.  They were posted by batboy if it helps.  I printed them out, but I can't find them in my mess.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||03-25-2000||07:03 PM||||The resistor in the tach will have to be replaced or swapped from the old one||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||03-25-2000||09:22 PM||||The tach's are different from 4cyl to V-6. You could swap resistor as Tom mentions or get a new 4cyl tach to keep the redline mark and numbers the same.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||03-26-2000||09:36 AM||||I forgot that '84 was a 4 cyl only year.||||reg||1
Z||000005||kevin||03-26-2000||09:11 PM||||Hey batboy, are you out there? Could you be so kind and post the wiring diagram that was mentioned above? I would really appreciate it. Thanks. ||||reg||14
